fix: tighten hero spacing, widen the demo, drop the orphan feature card

Three regressions/rough edges from the last pass:

- The demo sat 112px below the CTAs and fell entirely below the fold, so the
  hero ate a whole screen to say very little. Gap is now 40px and the demo is
  visible without scrolling, which is where the old app preview used to sit.
- The demo was a lone 600px card and read as a widget rather than the product.
  Widened to 860px and given a file-tree rail, so it looks like the app — and
  the backlink now visibly lands on "Zettelkasten method" in that tree, which
  makes the two-way link legible instead of just asserted.
- The features grid had 10 cards in 3 columns, leaving one stranded next to
  two empty cells. Removed "Embedded mind maps" as the most redundant of the
  set (canvas and the graph already cover visual thinking), leaving a clean 3x3.
